    "narrative": "Today\u2019s slate for **Ghost Ride the WHIP** is anchored by **Corbin Carroll**, who stands as our clear-cut elite play with a score of 83.53. Facing a favorable matchup against Grant Holmes, **Corbin Carroll** benefits from a strong lineup position and a positive platoon split; while the opposing pitcher's high hold rate tempers his stolen base potential slightly, his overall floor and ceiling combination remain untouchable. **Josh Naylor** (73.37) and **Seiya Suzuki** (67.75) also provide high-efficiency scoring, with **Josh Naylor** feasting on the weak xERA of Hayden Wesneski and **Seiya Suzuki** leveraging a park factor boost alongside a premium spot in the order. \n\nWe are emphasizing speed and situational advantage today, which keeps **Brice Turang** (64.79) in the starting lineup. **Brice Turang** draws a critical boost from a slow-delivering pitcher, maximizing his ability to hunt stolen bases, while the wind conditions further elevate his offensive ceiling. In terms of depth, **Travis Bazzana** was our most difficult cut; his 43.48 projection fell just short of the thresholds set by **Henry Bolte** and **Tyler Soderstrom**, who received significant score bumps due to favorable park factors against MacKenzie Gore. **Max Muncy** also sneaks into the starting nine at 55.64, primarily due to his high park factor and the ability to exploit a shaky opposing arm.\n\nRisk management remains a primary focus, as we are awaiting official lineups for nearly every active player. Users should monitor the status of **Gabriel Moreno** and **Isaac Paredes** specifically, as their projected production is heavily tied to their assumed positions in the batting order. We are maintaining caution with the bottom of our roster, particularly **Henry Bolte**, whose score of 48.54 is tethered to the assumption he hits ninth; any drop in that order placement will force a reassessment. We remain in a holding pattern for **James Wood**, **Vinnie Pasquantino**, and **Giancarlo Stanton**, all of whom are currently relegated to the bench due to their placement on the IL.",
